1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,173
Chunk-04.

2
00:00:01,173 --> 00:00:05,518
The doctor applied a cooling gel to the second-degree burns across my chest.

3
00:00:05,518 --> 00:00:09,169
He worked in silence, his eyes fixed strictly on the wounds.

4
00:00:09,169 --> 00:00:13,104
He knew better than to ask questions.The door opened.Ethan walked in.

5
00:00:13,104 --> 00:00:15,088
He had removed his tuxedo jacket.

6
00:00:15,088 --> 00:00:17,380
His white shirt was crisp, unblemished.

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,354
The chaos of the evening hadn't left a mark on him.

8
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:23,047
Not a drop of soup had touched him."How is she.

9
00:00:23,047 --> 00:00:24,518
" Ethan asked the doctor.

10
00:00:24,518 --> 00:00:26,029
He didn't look at my face.

11
00:00:26,029 --> 00:00:27,336
He looked at the burns.

12
00:00:27,336 --> 00:00:30,103
"She will heal," the doctor said, his voice low.

13
00:00:30,103 --> 00:00:31,309
"It will scar, though.

14
00:00:31,309 --> 00:00:32,606
The soup was boiling. "

15
00:00:32,606 --> 00:00:37,201
Ethan nodded, as if receiving a report on a damaged shipment of guns."Leave us. "

16
00:00:37,201 --> 00:00:39,486
The doctor slipped out of the room instantly.

17
00:00:39,486 --> 00:00:40,779
Ethan stepped closer.

18
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:47,113
The scent of his cologne-sandalwood and cold rain-mixed with the faint metallic tang of blood he always carried.

19
00:00:47,113 --> 00:00:50,129
It filled my nose, overpowering the sterile air.

20
00:00:50,129 --> 00:00:54,700
He reached out, his fingers hovering over the raw, blistered skin.I flinched.

21
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,466
His hand dropped to his side.

22
00:00:56,466 --> 00:00:59,169
"Ilene is sedated," he said.I didn't answer.

23
00:00:59,169 --> 00:01:03,941
The pain in my chest was a throbbing drumbeat, syncing with the rage building in my throat.

24
00:01:03,941 --> 00:01:07,002
"She didn't mean to do it, Rory.She saw the ring.

25
00:01:07,002 --> 00:01:08,292
It triggered an episode. "

26
00:01:08,292 --> 00:01:09,505
I looked at him then.

27
00:01:09,505 --> 00:01:15,829
I looked into the eyes of the man who ruled the underworld, the man who terrified the police and politicians alike.

28
00:01:15,829 --> 00:01:18,497
And I didn't see a monster.I saw a coward.

29
00:01:18,497 --> 00:01:22,609
"She threw boiling soup on me in a Michelin-star restaurant, Ethan.

30
00:01:22,609 --> 00:01:24,882
That wasn't an episode.That was assault. "

31
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:26,052
"Lower your voice. "

32
00:01:26,052 --> 00:01:26,601
"No. "

33
00:01:26,601 --> 00:01:31,662
I slid off the table, clutching the thin hospital gown to my chest to cover my exposure.

34
00:01:31,662 --> 00:01:32,831
"I want to go home. "

35
00:01:32,831 --> 00:01:36,296
"You can't go to the Estate," he said.My stomach dropped."Why. "

36
00:01:36,296 --> 00:01:38,373
"I moved Ilene into the Guest Wing.

37
00:01:38,373 --> 00:01:40,373
She needs constant supervision.

38
00:01:40,373 --> 00:01:43,220
The doctors say she is a flight risk if she's alone. "

39
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:47,628
I laughed.It was a dry, brittle sound, like dead leaves crushing underfoot.

40
00:01:47,628 --> 00:01:49,460
"So I am the one leaving.Again. "

41
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,120
"It's for your safety, Aurora. "

42
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,740
"Don't use that word," I snapped.My voice cracked.

43
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:55,998
"Don't you dare talk to me about safety.

44
00:01:55,998 --> 00:01:57,639
You are the Underboss.

45
00:01:57,639 --> 00:01:58,942
You command an army.

46
00:01:58,942 --> 00:02:02,351
You protect drug shipments, casinos, and politicians.

47
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:06,001
But you can't protect your wife from one five-foot-four mental patient. "

48
00:02:06,001 --> 00:02:10,529
Ethan grabbed my arm.His grip was iron."Watch your mouth.Ilene is family.

49
00:02:10,529 --> 00:02:12,378
Her father took a bullet for mine.

50
00:02:12,378 --> 00:02:13,501
I owe her my life. "

51
00:02:13,501 --> 00:02:16,263
"And what do you owe me." I whispered.He froze.

52
00:02:16,263 --> 00:02:19,903
His eyes searched mine, looking for the submissive girl he married.

53
00:02:19,903 --> 00:02:21,447
But she wasn't there anymore.

54
00:02:21,447 --> 00:02:23,418
She had burned away with the silk dress.

55
00:02:23,418 --> 00:02:26,166
"I owe you everything," he said, his voice rough.

56
00:02:26,166 --> 00:02:29,205
"That is why I am sending you to the penthouse downtown.

57
00:02:29,205 --> 00:02:30,414
You will be safe there. "

58
00:02:30,414 --> 00:02:31,778
He let go of my arm.

59
00:02:31,778 --> 00:02:32,954
He checked his watch.

60
00:02:32,954 --> 00:02:34,464
"I have to get back to her.

61
00:02:34,464 --> 00:02:37,144
She wakes up screaming if I'm not in the room. "

62
00:02:37,144 --> 00:02:38,556
He turned and walked out.

63
00:02:38,556 --> 00:02:44,016
He left his injured wife alone in a cold clinic to go hold the hand of the woman who burned her.

64
00:02:44,016 --> 00:02:45,083
I looked at the door.

65
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:47,949
The lock didn't keep people out.It kept me in.Chapter 3

66
00:02:47,949 --> 00:02:51,588
Instead of going to the penthouse, I took a cab straight to the Estate.

67
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:59,227
It was a fortress of stone and iron, built to withstand sieges from rival families, but the true enemy was already inside.

68
00:02:59,227 --> 00:03:03,366
I swept through the front doors, ignoring the shocked expressions of the guards.

69
00:03:03,366 --> 00:03:04,883
They didn't dare stop me.

70
00:03:04,883 --> 00:03:08,658
I was still the Donna, even if my husband treated me like a mistress.

71
00:03:08,658 --> 00:03:10,563
The house was quiet.Too quiet.

72
00:03:10,563 --> 00:03:12,326
I headed toward the main staircase.

73
00:03:12,326 --> 00:03:18,377
At the top of the landing, the gallery wall stretched out-a space that was supposed to be covered in our wedding photos.

74
00:03:18,377 --> 00:03:22,480
They were large, black-and-white prints of the day two crime families merged.

75
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,855
Now, the wall was bare.

76
00:03:23,855 --> 00:03:29,622
The frames lay shattered on the marble floor below, and glass crunched ominously under my heels.I looked up.

77
00:03:29,622 --> 00:03:31,740
Ilene stood at the top of the stairs.

78
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:36,057
She was wearing one of my silk robes, looking like a wraith-pale and smiling.

79
00:03:36,057 --> 00:03:38,366
"I thought they looked better down there," she said.
